Material taken from riemann-diagrams
(https://github.com/scottcochran/riemann-diagrams), at its commit
f87256e, copied and not imported: the drawing library
diagrams/src/lib.py (itself from TOPAK, Apache-2.0, as its header
says), diagrams/src/metrics.py, the font subsets in diagrams/src/fonts/,
tools/build-fonts.py and tools/measure-page.py. They keep the licence
they have there (Apache-2.0). The font subsets were rebuilt here, from
the same Noto sources, with six characters more (tools/build-fonts.py). LICENSE and LICENSE-DOCS are copied from
it too.

The fonts in diagrams/src/fonts/, which every poster embeds, are
subsets of Noto Sans, Noto Sans Mono and Noto Sans Math, Copyright
2022 The Noto Project Authors, licensed under the SIL Open Font
License, Version 1.1 (diagrams/src/fonts/OFL.txt). They are not this
repository's work and are covered by neither license above; the OFL
applies to the fonts, not to the posters drawn with them.

What the posters draw and quote from riemann-masullo is that project's,
licensed by it under the Apache License, Version 2.0 (its LICENSE and
README.md, "License"), and is used here under that licence, with this
notice as its attribution:

  * the Lean declaration names, files, lines, docstrings (their
    Paper:, Gap:, Classical input: and Deviation: lines, the last
    quoted on the declarations posters) and the dependencies
    between declarations, read at a pinned commit from its compiled
    library by its own scripts/progress/Deps.lean, and kept in
    diagrams/src/deps.json, a file derived from that project;
  * the text of ERRATA.md that the posters quote (items, entries,
    what is missing, how a step was settled, Checked values), and the
    targets and axioms of comparator.json.

Code that riemann-masullo vendors under RiemannMasullo/External/ keeps
its own licence and notices. diagrams/src/deps.json lists its
declarations' names and dependencies; the posters count them and draw
none of them.

The manuscript, A. M. Masullo, The Music of the Primes (draft of
2026-11-20), belongs to its author and is not covered by riemann-
masullo's licence or by this repository's. This repository does not
read, copy or quote it: the posters give item and page numbers as the
Lean docstrings and ERRATA.md give them, and check only the
manuscript's SHA-256 as riemann-masullo's paper/README.md states it.

A poster here says what the Lean formalisation rests on, at one commit.
It says nothing about whether the manuscript or the formalisation is
correct.

Third-party software is not part of this repository and is not covered
